description: |
    Some guest-related commands were missing correct environment. The
    fix changes the following:

    * commands that interact with a guest, invoked by tmt on the runner,
      including ``ssh`` or custom reboot commands, now inherit their
      environment from tmt process. This has been true for many of them
      already, but we identified commands that did not inherit this
      environment, especially ``ssh`` and custom reboot commands supported
      by the :ref:`/plugins/provision/connect` plugin.
    * ``SendEnv`` SSH option can no longer be set by a ``provision``
      phase unless in the "feeling safe" mode; this prevents users from
      leaking environment variables exposed to ``ssh`` processes by changing
      their plans.
